{
  "name": "Normalise Contact Mobile Numbers",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Normalise Contact Mobile Numbers\n\nWhenever a Contact is created or updated in Administrate, this normalises that contact's **mobile** number to international (E.164) format.\n\n**IMPORTANT - country rules:** the defaults in **Config** are for **UK mobiles only** (country code 44, trunk prefix 0, mobiles start with 7). Numbers that do not match the configured country are left untouched. Change the Config values for another country; one country per workflow.\n\n**Flow**\n1. **Contact Created / Contact Updated** - Administrate webhook triggers (registered by the trigger nodes).\n2. **Config** - country rules and the log Data Table ID.\n3. **Get Contact** - reads that contact's phone numbers.\n4. **Normalize Contact** - for usage = mobile, e.g. 07... -> +447..., 0044 -> +44, 44 -> +44, strips spaces/brackets/dashes/dots and drops a trunk 0 after the country code (+44 (0)7... -> +447...). Emits an item ONLY if the number changes.\n5. **Update Mobile (Webhook)** - writes the corrected number. Other phone types (office/home/fax) are untouched.\n6. **Log (Webhook)** - records the change in the 'Phone Normalization Log' Data Table.\n\nLoop-safe: the update re-fires 'Contact Updated', but the second pass finds the number already correct and stops.\n",
        "height": 720,
        "width": 660,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "9bf5cf51-f3a0-4c99-9ebd-5eb4f1c87ab0",
      "name": "Sticky - Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "https://api.getadministrate.com/graphql",
        "authentication": "predefinedCredentialType",
        "nodeCredentialType": "administrateOAuth2Api",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ ({ \"query\": \"query($id: ID!) { node(id: $id) { ... on Contact { id personalName { firstName lastName } phoneNumbers { usage number } } } }\", \"variables\": { \"id\": $json.payload.node.id } }) }}",
        "options": {
          "response": {
            "response": {
              "neverError": true
            }
          }
        }
      },
      "id": "45b8386c-185f-4fa4-9dba-0b76b273a092",
      "name": "Get Contact",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.4,
      "position": [
        320,
        1152
      ],
      "credentials": {
        "administrateOAuth2Api": {
          "id": "",
          "name": "Administrate OAuth2"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Country rules come from the Config node. Defaults are for UK mobiles (+44, trunk 0, mobiles start 7).\nconst cfg = $('Config').first().json;\nconst CC = String(cfg.COUNTRY_CODE || \"\").replace(/^\\+/, \"\");\nconst INTL = String(cfg.INTERNATIONAL_DIAL_PREFIX || \"\");\nconst TRUNK = String(cfg.TRUNK_PREFIX || \"\");\nconst MOBILE_START = String(cfg.MOBILE_NATIONAL_PREFIX || \"\");\nconst ACCEPT_BARE_CC = cfg.ACCEPT_BARE_COUNTRY_CODE === true || String(cfg.ACCEPT_BARE_COUNTRY_CODE).toLowerCase() === \"true\";\nif (!CC) throw new Error(\"Config.COUNTRY_CODE is empty\");\n\nconst normalizeNumber = (raw) => {\n  if (raw == null) return raw;\n  const s = String(raw).trim();\n  if (s === \"\") return s;\n  const c = s.replace(/[\\s()\\-.]/g, \"\");\n  let national = null;\n  if (c.startsWith(\"+\" + CC)) national = c.slice(1 + CC.length);\n  else if (INTL && c.startsWith(INTL + CC)) national = c.slice(INTL.length + CC.length);\n  else if (ACCEPT_BARE_CC && c.startsWith(CC)) national = c.slice(CC.length);\n  else if (TRUNK && c.startsWith(TRUNK + MOBILE_START)) national = c.slice(TRUNK.length);\n  else return s;\n  // drop any trunk prefix written after the country code, e.g. +44 (0)7... -> +447...\n  while (TRUNK && national.startsWith(TRUNK)) national = national.slice(TRUNK.length);\n  if (national === \"\") return s;\n  return \"+\" + CC + national;\n};\nconst out = [];\nconst runAt = new Date().toISOString();\nfor (const item of $input.all()) {\n  const n = item.json && item.json.data && item.json.data.node;\n  if (!n) continue;\n  const phones = Array.isArray(n.phoneNumbers) ? n.phoneNumbers : [];\n  const idx = phones.findIndex(p => String((p && p.usage) || \"\").toLowerCase() === \"mobile\");\n  if (idx === -1) continue;\n  const usage = phones[idx].usage;\n  const oldNum = phones[idx].number;\n  const newNum = normalizeNumber(oldNum);\n  if (newNum == null || newNum === oldNum) continue;\n  const mutation = \"mutation { contact { update(input: { contactId: \" + JSON.stringify(n.id) + \", phoneNumbers: [{usage: \" + usage + \", number: \" + JSON.stringify(newNum) + \"}] }) { contact { id } errors { label message value } } } }\";\n  const nm = (((n.personalName && n.personalName.firstName) || \"\") + \" \" + ((n.personalName && n.personalName.lastName) || \"\")).trim();\n  out.push({ json: { contactId: n.id, contactName: nm, oldNumber: oldNum, newNumber: newNum, runAt: runAt, requestBody: JSON.stringify({ query: mutation }) } });\n}\nreturn out;"
      },
